# ============================================================
#  Midnight heists (threads 1, docs/threads-1-plan.md Part C): two stealing mini-delves, the Restricted Stacks
#  (heists/stacks.grim) and the seventh tower (heists/tower.grim). Like the Whisperwood delve (whisperwood/delve.grim),
#  but quiet: guile checks (deceive past people, feats using guile on locks, shelves and boards), now and then a
#  research or a spell check, never a fight or a negotiation; midnight only. The Cartographers' Master Map opens them
#  (heist_stacks_known, heist_tower_known; content/events/cartographers.grim).
#
#  Counters, reset on entry: heist_where (1 the stacks, 2 the tower), heist_depth (how deep or high), heist_loot (what
#  you carry), heist_cover (slips you can survive: 1, +1 with a prefect's round times, +1 more for the place's own
#  advantage). heist_stacks_deepest and heist_tower_highest persist.
#  Each step: left slips away with what you carry (heist_way_out); right goes on (heist_depth += 1, maybe loot, next).
#  A lost check queues heist_slip while cover lasts (cover, health or loot pay for it; a word may reach a prefect),
#  else heist_caught (the loot is taken, a month of detention, and the prefects' notice escalates as night_suspicion's
#  does: watched, then locked out; outrunning them leaves only the morning's word). A hazard marked ⚠ goes straight to
#  heist_caught. Stealing is a little Hollow, paid at the way out.
# ============================================================

@event heist_way_out
title: Out Before Dawn
trigger: queued
class: story
tone: tense
repeat: 1
art: pouch
tags: danger money
scene: A student slipping out of a dark doorway at the grey end of night, a bundle held under one arm, looking both ways down a castle corridor.
text: {heist_loot == 0: {heist_deck_tonight == 1: You come out with nothing to sell but a tin of cards that was never yours to sell, and a grin.|You come out with nothing but dust on your knees and your heart going like a drum.}|{heist_loot <= 2: You come out with a few small, old things under your shirt, each worth more than it looks.|{heist_loot <= 4: You come out with a real bundle: {heist_where == 1: pages, and something heavier that sighs when you move|papers, and something heavier that clinks when you move}.|You come out with more than your shirt will hold, and walk very carefully.}}} {heist_where == 1: The library is grey with dawn behind you.|The tower's slits are going grey above you.}
> left: Sell it to the collector
  hint: Crowns, by what you carry. A little Hollow.
  if heist_loot >= 1:
    alignment -tiny
  if heist_loot >= 6:
    gold +huge
  elif heist_loot >= 4:
    gold +large
  elif heist_loot >= 2:
    gold +medium
  elif heist_loot >= 1:
    gold +small
  say: {heist_loot == 0: {heist_deck_tonight == 1: The tin goes to Corvin, not the collector. You go to bed, and lie awake grinning.|There's nothing to sell. You go to bed, and lie awake anyway.}|{~The collector in the village back room weighs each thing in a gloved hand and pays in old crowns, without a question.|The collector's man meets you by the village pump at noon. He counts your things, and then his coins, and both counts are fair.|The collector holds your best piece up to the window and is quiet for a long time. Then he pays more than you'd have asked.}}
  if heist_where == 1 and heist_depth > heist_stacks_deepest:
    heist_stacks_deepest = heist_depth
  if heist_where == 2 and heist_depth > heist_tower_highest:
    heist_tower_highest = heist_depth
  heist_depth = 0
  heist_loot = 0
  heist_deck_tonight = 0
> right: Keep it, and read it
  hint: Lore, by what you carry. A little Hollow.
  if heist_loot >= 1:
    alignment -tiny
  if heist_loot >= 6:
    lore +large
    guile +small
  elif heist_loot >= 4:
    lore +medium
  elif heist_loot >= 2:
    lore +small
  elif heist_loot >= 1:
    lore +tiny
  say: {heist_loot == 0: There's nothing to keep but the night, and you keep that.|{~You spread it all on your bed behind drawn curtains and read until breakfast. Half of it you shouldn't know. You know it now.|You hide it under a loose floorboard and take it out a piece at a time, over weeks, like a box of sweets.|You read it all twice and burn the worst of it. The rest you keep, and it keeps you up.}}
  if heist_where == 1 and heist_depth > heist_stacks_deepest:
    heist_stacks_deepest = heist_depth
  if heist_where == 2 and heist_depth > heist_tower_highest:
    heist_tower_highest = heist_depth
  heist_depth = 0
  heist_loot = 0
  heist_deck_tonight = 0

@event heist_slip
title: A Near Thing
trigger: queued
class: story
tone: tense
repeat: 1
art: lantern
tags: danger
scene: A student flattened into a dark alcove, holding their breath, as the glow of a lantern slides past along the floor.
on_show:
  heist_cover -= 1
  health -tiny
  heist_dropped = 0
  if heist_loot > 0:
    heist_loot -= 1
    heist_dropped = 1
text: {heist_dropped == 1: {~You get away, just, and something you carried doesn't: it's lying out there in the dark where you dropped it.|You end up flat in an alcove with your heart in your mouth and one thing fewer in your shirt.|You're clear, scraped and shaking, and you've left something behind for somebody to find.}|{~You get away, just, with nothing to lose but your nerve, and some of that.|You end up flat in an alcove with your heart in your mouth, glad your shirt was empty.|You're clear, scraped and shaking, and you've left nothing behind but a scuff.}} {heist_cover > 0: You've one more near thing in you, maybe.|That was your last near thing.}
> left: That's enough for tonight
  queue heist_way_out now
  say: {~You take what's left and go, by the long way.|You decide the night has made its point.|You go while you can.}
> right: Wait, and go on
  hint: On: the next slip may not be a near thing.
  queue night_suspicion chance unlikely
  if heist_where == 1:
    queue any in heist_stacks now
  else:
    queue any in heist_tower now
  say: {~You wait till the dark is quiet again, and go on.|You count to five hundred, and go on.|You go on. Somewhere behind you, someone is looking at the place where you were.}

@event heist_caught
title: Caught
trigger: queued
class: story
tone: grim
repeat: 1
art: eye
tags: danger crisis
scene: A prefect's lantern held high in a dark doorway, lighting up a student caught with a bundle of stolen things in their arms.
on_show:
  if heist_where == 1 and heist_depth > heist_stacks_deepest:
    heist_stacks_deepest = heist_depth
  if heist_where == 2 and heist_depth > heist_tower_highest:
    heist_tower_highest = heist_depth
  heist_depth = 0
  heist_deck_tonight = 0
  heist_warned = 0
  if has(watched):
    heist_warned = 1
text: A lantern comes up full in your face. {heist_where == 1: Down in the stacks, at night,|Halfway up the seventh tower, at night,} {heist_loot == 0: and empty-handed, which convinces nobody.|with your arms full of things that aren't yours. The prefect takes them all, into a sack for the confiscation vault.} The prefect behind the lantern looks less angry than tired.
> left: Go quietly
  gain detention
  mood -small
  if has(watched):
    lose watched
    gain locked_out
  else:
    gain watched
  heist_loot = 0
  say: {heist_warned == 1: You go quietly. You'd been warned: a month of detention, and three of a door that is checked at midnight.|You go quietly. It doesn't help much: a month of detention, starting with the first free afternoon, and your name on the prefects' list.}
> right: Run for it
  challenge feat using guile journeyman:
    win:
      health -tiny
      mood -small
      heist_loot = 0
      queue night_suspicion now
      say: {heist_loot == 0: You run, and know every turn better than they do. You get away. You also know they saw your face.|You leave the sack to the prefect and run, and know every turn better than they do. You get away. You also know they saw your face.}
    lose:
      gain detention
      health -small
      mood -small
      if has(watched):
        lose watched
        gain locked_out
      else:
        gain watched
      heist_loot = 0
      say: {heist_warned == 1: You run two corridors and into a second prefect. You'd been warned: a month of detention, three of a locked door at midnight, and a bruised shin.|You run two corridors and into a second prefect. A month of detention, a bruised shin, and your name on the prefects' list.}
